---
// Two panels over the same three arms: how many prompt tokens each arm sent,
// and how much of that arrived uncached at full price. A single stacked bar
// would hide the second measure entirely, since the full-price slice is 1.7%
// to 7.4% of the bar and would render as a two-pixel sliver.
const rows = [
  { arm: 'off',      total: 215, share: 1.7 },
  { arm: 'on-cache', total: 191, share: 2.1 },
  { arm: 'on-token', total: 132, share: 7.4 },
];
const TOTAL_MAX = 230; // 215M plus headroom, so no bar touches the right edge
const SHARE_MAX = 8;
const pitch = 46;
const pct = (v, max) => (v / max) * 100;
---
<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig-pair">
    <div>
      <p class="fig-head">total prompt tokens</p>
      <p class="fig-sub">cache reads plus fresh input</p>
      <svg height="156" role="img" aria-labelledby="ts-a-t ts-a-d">
        <title id="ts-a-t">Total prompt tokens by arm: off 215M, on-cache 191M, on-token 132M.</title>
        <desc id="ts-a-d">Horizontal bars on a shared scale from zero to 230 million. Token mode sends the fewest tokens.</desc>
        {rows.map((r, i) => (
          <g>
            <text class="t-name" x="0" y={14 + i * pitch}>{r.arm}</text>
            <text class="t-val" x="100%" y={14 + i * pitch} text-anchor="end">{r.total}M</text>
            <rect class="m-blue" x="0" y={20 + i * pitch} width={`${pct(r.total, TOTAL_MAX)}%`} height="12" rx="4" />
            <rect class="m-blue" x="0" y={20 + i * pitch} width="4" height="12" />
          </g>
        ))}
        <line class="grid" x1="0" x2="100%" y1="134.5" y2="134.5" />
        <text class="t-ax" x="0" y="150">0</text>
        <text class="t-ax" x="43.478%" y="150" text-anchor="middle">100M</text>
        <text class="t-ax" x="86.957%" y="150" text-anchor="middle">200M</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="fig-head">share billed at full price</p>
      <p class="fig-sub">fresh input, never cached</p>
      <svg height="156" role="img" aria-labelledby="ts-b-t ts-b-d">
        <title id="ts-b-t">Share of prompt tokens billed at full price: off 1.7%, on-cache 2.1%, on-token 7.4%.</title>
        <desc id="ts-b-d">Horizontal bars on a scale from zero to eight percent. Token mode's full-price share is more than four times the baseline's.</desc>
        {rows.map((r, i) => (
          <g>
            <text class="t-name" x="0" y={14 + i * pitch}>{r.arm}</text>
            <text class="t-val" x="100%" y={14 + i * pitch} text-anchor="end">{r.share}%</text>
            <rect class="m-warm" x="0" y={20 + i * pitch} width={`${pct(r.share, SHARE_MAX)}%`} height="12" rx="4" />
            <rect class="m-warm" x="0" y={20 + i * pitch} width="4" height="12" />
          </g>
        ))}
        <line class="grid" x1="0" x2="100%" y1="134.5" y2="134.5" />
        <text class="t-ax" x="0" y="150">0</text>
        <text class="t-ax" x="50%" y="150" text-anchor="middle">4%</text>
        <text class="t-ax" x="100%" y="150" text-anchor="end">8%</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    Compression works on the left panel and backfires on the right. Token mode sends <b>39% fewer</b> prompt
    tokens than baseline, and <b>4.4x</b> as large a share of them arrives uncached, where they bill at ten
    times the cache-read rate.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
